# BCT Delivery Flow

Use this as the default for BCT changes unless the user explicitly narrows or
overrides the scope.

1. Before changing anything, record the intended files, permitted deployment
   boundary, E2E success criteria, and protected UNKNOWN operations/claims.
2. Complete the focused regression, full test suite, static checks, and diff
   check locally as one verification recipe before opening CI.
3. Keep a coherent correction and its regression coverage in one PR. While CI
   runs, prepare the exact-SHA deployment, rollback, and E2E inputs without
   changing LIVE.
4. After an exact-head CI pass, verify the exact SHA through deployment and
   advance E2E only in order: deployment health, one round trip, durable
   receipt/recovery, then the larger orchestration scenario.
5. Use compact status or presence for routine health. Request full DOM or RCC
   state only for a diagnosis, and label stale or uncertain observations rather
   than treating them as IDLE.
6. On a failed external effect, preserve the receipt and collect evidence
   (canonical text, DOM, ACK, active execution, pending receipt) before any
   retry. Never replay an UNKNOWN effect or release a protected claim merely
   to make progress.
7. Parallelize read-only inspection, test preparation, and GitHub observation.
   Keep shared worktree writes, browser sends, and LIVE mutations serialized.

Report the final state with the exact tested SHA, test/CI evidence, LIVE
evidence, E2E result, and any deferred follow-ups.
